  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 150 PM EDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThe extended period begins where the short term leaves off with a \nfairly dominate 596dm 500mb mid level ridge centered over the TN \nValley.  As a result, afternoon highs will continue reach up into \nthe mid 90s most locations ...except mountains.   Heat index values \nwill flirt with Heat Advisory for central and eastern GA Thu, Fri \nand especially Saturday.  \n\nAll of the medium range guidance is in good agreement that \nreinforcing and much stronger northern stream trough will dig \nsoutheast through the mid Atlantic and begin to break down the \neastern periphery of the ridge by Saturday.   This will drive a \nbackdoor front through the region late Saturday into Sunday.  POPs \ndo increase for the weekend both as a result of less of a \nsuppressive ridge and because of the enhancement along the \napproaching frontal boundary...which could take the form of a \nconvective complex Saturday afternoon/evening. About the only \nnoticeable sensible change will be a change in wind direction to the \nN or NE by Sunday and increased afternoon/evening thunderstorm \nactivity with the center of the ridge pushed back to the west of TX \nand a broad NW flow in place across the SE through the remainder of \nthe extended.   Afternoon highs could come down somewhat by Monday \nas more afternoon activity is expected.  NBM guidance reflects that \nwith highs only touching 90 on Labor Day and widespread 20-40\npops.",
